{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/457568-changeling-the-dreaming-question","id":457568,"title":"Changeling the dreaming question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-25T18:43:09-07:00","id":457568,"title":"Changeling the dreaming question","content":"How different in gameplay are changeling the dreaming 1st ed and 2nd edition? Are the rules vastly different or is it just different in wording and types of can trips? Sadly I can't afford 2nd edition right now and would like to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5480-jonnyspiral","name":"Jonnyspiral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T19:12:42-07:00","id":457583,"title":"","content":"There are some pretty significant differences between first and second edition. There are a lot more ways for creatures of dream to directly affect the autumn realm. Damage got split into chimerical and real. The Arts got reworked a good bit.<br /> <br /> The most significant difference though is the rules for casting cantrips. In first edition, you used a combination of art, realm, and bunk cards to produce effects. In second edition, the system was redone to use dice instead of cards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T05:56:15-07:00","id":457964,"title":"","content":"Would the nice downloadable QuickStart for changeling cover the changes (just not in as much detail)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5480-jonnyspiral","name":"Jonnyspiral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T08:40:24-07:00","id":458078,"title":"","content":"That's a good question. I haven't looked at the quick start in over a decade, so I really don't remember what was in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T03:59:55-07:00","id":469279,"title":"","content":"I'll use this topic, if no one minds.<br /> <br /> What do we know about changeling society in Canada? Do Canada even exists in old World of Darkness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T04:56:33-07:00","id":469287,"title":"","content":"It exists and for Changelings it is Kingdom of Northern Ice, if I recall correctly, ruled by Queen of Laurels, again if I remember correctly, but that is pretty much all I can dredge up from my memory at the moment. For the most part I'd say, but like said I really do not recall how correct this assumption is, the society there is similar to the US as whole North America is part of the Concordia so all the problems inherent in it apply. Mostly ruled by Nobles under the now, if following metaplot, disappeared High King David and the Parliament of Dreams. This also means that it is inhabited by both Kithain and the Nunnehi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T07:18:43-07:00","id":469325,"title":"","content":"There's not a whole lot about the Kingdom of Northern Ice, if I recall correctly. The only real substance about it that I can remember is in Nobles The Shining Host with it's write up of Queen Laurel. She is a member of House Fiona. She is described as the most passionate and tempestuous of Concordia's monarchs but firmly seelie. She is reknowned as both a sorceress and a singer. She is &quot;part owner of a major Canadian metropolitan opera company.&quot;<br /> <br /> She also has what is described as a roller coaster love affair/arranged marriage with a Shadow Court lord named Duke Rococo. It says there are rumors that he is manipulating her with the goal of eventual Shadow Court takeover of Canada, but in truth, she is the one who is converting him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T08:28:47-07:00","id":469364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/457568-changeling-the-dreaming-question?p=469325#post469325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says there are rumors that he is manipulating her with the goal of eventual Shadow Court takeover of Canada, but in truth, she is the one who is converting him.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Fiona you can't be too sure about this. Thanks. So, Canada, I mean, Knigdom of Northern Ice is part of Concordia and is subject to High King?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T16:57:07-07:00","id":469676,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's right there in the map of Concordia on the end papers in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T21:44:54-07:00","id":472152,"title":"","content":"What happens to a Changeling who's banality caps out? Do they become humans, or do they die? I'm not entirely clear on whether Changelings are half human, or if they're human bodies with Fae souls or what's going on with that. I think I remember one piece of information saying that Changelings could be reborn into a new body after their deaths (thus becoming Childlings again), but I don't know if that's accurate or not.<br /> <br /> I think Changeling sounds pretty depressing otherwise. You're born with the power of imagination and creativity, gradually lose your power as you grow up, until eventually you lose your creativity entirely. But if there's a way to hit the reset button, then it might not be so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-08-2015, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:08:57-07:00","id":472980,"title":"","content":"They become, for most intents and purposes, a normal human who forgets everything about the Dreaming. They CAN recover; their Changeling soul is still there. But it takes a massive infusion of Glamour (with no specific mechanics other than that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:57:19-07:00","id":473053,"title":"","content":"Ah, that's kind of disturbing. There are still vampires, werewolves, mages, demons, wraiths and who knows what else that now consider them a tasty snack... Plus the possibility of Hunters who don't know they're human and still wish to kill them. D:<br /> <br /> <br /> Still doesn't answer the question regarding the chance to be reborn after death. Kind of hard to imagine centuries after disbelief in them occured, there are still Fae floating around looking for bodies for the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:40:58-07:00","id":473101,"title":"","content":"When a changeling gets overwhelmed by banality, the changeling becomes undone. That is, the faerie portion of the changeling's soul goes dormant and they forget everything about glamour and the chimerical world. Usually when this happens, an infusion of glamour or contact with the chimerical is enough to reawaken a changeling's faerie half. If a changeling's permanent banality reaches 10, the changeling becomes permanently undone. After that, nothing can reawaken the faerie portion of the changeling's soul. The changeling is too weighed down by banality for the faerie half to resurface.<br /> <br /> Once the changeling dies, the changeling's human half goes on to what ever fate awaits humans after death. Thanks to the changeling way ritual enacted shortly after the shattering, the changeling's faerie half mixes with a new human soul and gets reborn as a new changeling. The reborn part of that is literal - changeling's aren't body snatchers, and faeries souls don't go floating around looking for new bodies to inhabit.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of exceptions to that. Most sidhe think that the changeling way didn't apply to them. They point out that there have been no confirmed sidhe reincarnations since the resurgence as proof. My personal fanon is that sidhe, wether they like it or not, are bound by the changeling way ritual. There just hasn't been enough time since the resurgence to confirm a reincarnation yet. Changeling memory is a funny thing and the mists are fickle. A sidhe could easily have reincarnated in that time period but not remember their previous life and go unrecognized by surviving changelings. See Niall Peacemaker for an example of a sidhe who didn't even die yet is unknown by all the changelings he encounters.<br /> <br /> The other exception is the adhene, the kithain's opposite number during the War of Trees. The adhene were banned from earth by the time the shattering happened, and never enacted their own version of the changeling way ritual. Any adhene on earth is in precarious position and most will seek out a human body to protect themselves against the onslaught of banality. Because of this, the mechanics of how they are affected by banality are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:27:35-07:00","id":473333,"title":"","content":"Well I wasn't talking about them retaining their memories, just whether or not it was possible for them to &quot;cheat&quot; death to a certain degree, and it sounds like they can, if I read your comment right. Kingdoms of Amalur had a similar system in that while the Fae could be killed, they didn't stay dead. It could take anywhere from a few hours to a few centuries, but eventually the Fae managed to return to the mortal world when their bodies were destroyed. Except the Fae in that game were manifestations of nature, rather than dreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of reviewers give Dreaming flak because the artwork and stuff doesn't hold in theme to the WoD, but when I pause and think about the premise of the game, it's actually very depressing and possesses the horror elements that earn it a place in the WoD series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T14:49:29-07:00","id":491951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/457568-changeling-the-dreaming-question?p=473101#post473101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">changeling's aren't body snatchers, and faeries souls don't go floating around looking for new bodies to inhabit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... there's the sidhe... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T17:26:58-07:00","id":492114,"title":"","content":"Depends on which books you read. They didn't really become body snatchers until the Arthaus era. Even then, the idea of them being body snatchers doesn't really fit with the mechanics. If they were truly body snatchers, I'd expect them to operate more like the Adhene. That's why my fannon has them being under the changeling way ritual but either not knowing it or not wanting to admit they're in the same league as the commoner kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T09:54:51-07:00","id":492670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/457568-changeling-the-dreaming-question?p=469279#post469279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll use this topic, if no one minds.<br /> <br /> What do we know about changeling society in Canada? Do Canada even exists in old World of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Hunter the reckoning player i will just say this.<br /> <br /> &quot;We Dont Go To Canada.&quot;<br /> Dijon..just...New Dijon.... Still gives me nightmares","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}